# Review findings and recurring code habits

Merge-gate / quota / when-to-request → `pr-review-merge.mdc` + `CONTRIBUTING.md`. Issues → `github-issues.mdc`.

## Disposition triad (every actionable finding)

Never leave hanging (threads **and** outside-diff / summary nits):

1. **Fix** → resolve thread
2. **Wontfix** → short PR reply + resolve
3. **Defer** → open follow-up issue, link from PR reply, resolve

## `Refs` vs `Closes` / stubs

- Incomplete acceptance / deepen-in-progress → `Refs #N`, never `Closes`
- Stubs / `assert!(… \|\| true)` / “smoke only” ≠ done

## Durable habits

- Check all callers and GUI hosts when changing shared APIs, public fields, FFI, or host options. Run the relevant living-room/release gate when those paths are affected.
- Test observable outcomes with meaningful preconditions; ROM-dependent tests skip cleanly when ROMs are absent. Do not stub success or discard I/O errors.
- Preserve hardware timing and cross-frame state; convenience tape paths must still load correctly.
- Keep ABI/header and packaging versions in sync when changing those surfaces. Pin GitHub Actions to full commit SHAs.
